<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-20T00:11:09+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Sun, 20 Sep 2026 00:11:09 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[1897 park could get $49 mn golf course makeover 129 years after Congress set it aside for public use]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134333304.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Congress created Washington’s East Potomac Park for public recreation in 1897, and its golf course opened in 1919. Now, the Trump administration is moving ahead with plans to renovate the historic public course into a major golf venue. A $389,355 contract has been awarded for environmental and preservation work, while a construction contract could be worth up to $49 million.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/congress-set-aside-washingtons-east-potomac-land-for-public-recreation-in-1897-129-years-later-a-plan-costing-up-to-49-million-could-transform-its-public-golf-course-into-a-championship-venue/articleshow/134333304.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/congress-set-aside-washingtons-east-potomac-land-for-public-recreation-in-1897-129-years-later-a-plan-costing-up-to-49-million-could-transform-its-public-golf-course-into-a-championship-venue/articleshow/134333304.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T23:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134333772,imgsize-138523.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[California farming family challenged a second-home rule in 2017; 9 years later, Supreme Court declines]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134334182.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After a prolonged legal battle, a California family has seen their hopes of purchasing a second home on agricultural land dashed. In June 2026, the US Supreme Court decided not to review their appeal, upholding Marin County's regulations that require agricultural covenants for new homes. This ruling marks the conclusive end to the family's challenge against established land-use restrictions in California's courts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2017-a-california-farming-family-began-fighting-a-rule-tying-a-second-home-on-267-acres-to-future-commercial-farming-nine-years-later-the-us-supreme-court-declined-to-hear-the-appeal/articleshow/134334182.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2017-a-california-farming-family-began-fighting-a-rule-tying-a-second-home-on-267-acres-to-future-commercial-farming-nine-years-later-the-us-supreme-court-declined-to-hear-the-appeal/articleshow/134334182.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T23:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creat