st 18th-century building]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134331073.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/in-1995-strange-marks-appeared-in-a-photograph-of-an-english-estate-31-years-later-archaeologists-say-they-may-have-uncovered-the-foundations-of-a-lost-18th-century-building/articleshow/134331073.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/in-1995-strange-marks-appeared-in-a-photograph-of-an-english-estate-31-years-later-archaeologists-say-they-may-have-uncovered-the-foundations-of-a-lost-18th-century-building/articleshow/134331073.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T23:01:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134331315,imgsize-321099.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Black Eye Galaxy Image: Webb and Hubble reveal dusty star-forming band; traces ancient merger]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134330971.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Located roughly 17 million light-years from Earth in the constellation Coma Berenices, M64 is known for an unusual internal motion: gas in its outer regions rotates in the opposite direction to the gas and stars closer to the centre. NASA says this counter-rotation may be a remnant of a merger involving M64 and a smaller satellite galaxy more than a billion years ago.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/nasas-webb-telescope-captured-the-black-eye-galaxy-in-unprecedented-detail-its-opposing-gas-streams-reveal-a-violent-cosmic-past/articleshow/134330971.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/s