]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2015-a-connecticut-carpenter-and-his-wife-bought-5-acres-in-upstate-new-york-for-27000-he-built-three-cabins-and-the-rentals-generated-more-than-2-1-million/articleshow/134338499.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2015-a-connecticut-carpenter-and-his-wife-bought-5-acres-in-upstate-new-york-for-27000-he-built-three-cabins-and-the-rentals-generated-more-than-2-1-million/articleshow/134338499.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-19T22:04:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134338667,imgsize-606536.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Canada confirms first spotted lanternfly in Windsor, after invasive insect spreads across 18 US states]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134332837.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Canada confirmed its first spotted lanternfly detection in Windsor, Ontario.  Movement restrictions are now in place to prevent further spread of this invasive species.  Surrounding areas are under surveillance to assess the infestation's extent.  This pest poses significant risks to agriculture and forestry industries.  Early detection and reporting are crucial for managing its impact.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/an-invasive-insect-first-found-in-pennsylvania-in-2014-spread-across-18-us-states-canada-has-now-confirmed-its-first-spotted-lanternfly-detection-in-windsor-putting-grape-growing-regions-on-alert/articleshow/134332837.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/an-invasive-insect-first-found-in-pennsylvania-in-2014-spread-across-18-us-states-canada-has-now-confirmed-its-first-spotted-lanternfly-detection-in-windso